WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.859
- Let's say hello to Mikey Day, everybody.

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:07.859
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:28.391 --> 00:00:30.114
- Sweet, I like your outfit.

00:00:30.114 --> 00:00:31.305
- Thank you, you too.

00:00:31.305 --> 00:00:34.136
- Yeah, nice threads.
Okay, so you've been here-

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:36.210
- You have me on with an icon,

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.310
telling awesome Elvis stories.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.096
- I know, what are you
bringing to the table, Mikey?

00:00:40.096 --> 00:00:42.540
- Nothing. Nothing.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.740
- No, I have to ask this though,

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.670
'cause I'm new to the building.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.946
I love working here.

00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:46.779
- It's awesome.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:47.714
- You, yeah.
- Welcome.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:48.789
- Yes, so do you love it?

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:50.572
Do you have like your favorite places?

00:00:50.572 --> 00:00:55.572
- Yeah, it's fun seeing NBC
like, news casters in the lobby.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:01.790
I've seen Lester Holt, just
walking in jeans, which is-

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.203
- [Kelly] Which trips you out.

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:05.912
- You're like, "you don't own jeans."

00:01:05.912 --> 00:01:08.100
(audience and guests laugh)
You were born in a suit.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.620
So, Rachel Maddow, I've seen.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.570
- At the Starbucks.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.650
- Down below.
- I know that

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.850
Starbucks, the subway Starbucks.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.350
- Right, the subway Starbucks.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:18.180
- Have you ever been in
there like, really early?

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.430
I had a early call time,
it was like 6 something AM.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.110
They were blasting music, I was like-

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:23.943
- Oh really?

00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:25.634
- Like, it was like a rave.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:26.804
(audience and guests laughing)

00:01:26.804 --> 00:01:27.637
- And you were like-

00:01:27.637 --> 00:01:30.180
- I looked at these two and
I was like, "It's 6 AM, bro."

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.770
I was like, that's early.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.570
- But, was it Kelly Clarkson music?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.219
- No, not even my music.

00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:37.496
- Then I'm not going, it's
your music or nothing.

00:01:37.496 --> 00:01:39.415
Your music or nothing!

00:01:39.415 --> 00:01:40.482
- It was actually good.

00:01:40.482 --> 00:01:43.566
♪ Some people wait a lifetime ♪

00:01:43.566 --> 00:01:45.273
♪ For a moment like this ♪
(audience cheers)

00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:48.840
- You know what? It would've
been more acceptable at 6 AM.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.471
- I watched that and almost cried.

00:01:50.471 --> 00:01:51.810
- Oh, I did cry.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.037
- Well, I was like, "Kelly
deserves it so much."

00:01:55.037 --> 00:01:56.471
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:01:56.471 --> 00:01:57.750
"Kelly is a star."

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.583
- Thank you!

00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:00.840
- I was, I remember I was in college.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.504
- I was just telling her
the first season of "Idol,"

00:02:03.504 --> 00:02:05.460
they have a person every week, too

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.960
and ours was Burt Bacharach.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.100
- [Mikey] Oh, really?
- That came on that week.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.420
Yeah, and we did Burt Bacharach songs.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.843
I did "Walk On By", before Doja.

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:14.777
- Before Doja. Before Doja.
- That's right.

00:02:14.777 --> 00:02:15.720
- Because, I don't know if she was alive.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.054
I'm a lot older than her.

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:17.887
(audience and guests laugh)

00:02:17.887 --> 00:02:19.440
So wait, I've been on SNL

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.530
and I will say the most
upsetting thing for me to watch

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.760
is, I'm there all day, right?

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.552
Even as a musical guest,
you're there all day, right?

00:02:25.552 --> 00:02:26.385
- [Mikey] Right.

00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:28.380
- And you watch all these skits get cut.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.213
- [Mikey] Oh yeah.

00:02:29.213 --> 00:02:31.320
- So, like what, and I
mean and like funny ones!

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.577
Like, sometimes y'all will
keep some, and I'm like,

00:02:33.577 --> 00:02:34.687
"Why did you keep that one over that one?"

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.238
I'm like, "I liked that one."

00:02:36.238 --> 00:02:37.207
- That always happens.

00:02:37.207 --> 00:02:38.220
"Why did you cut that?"

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.760
- Yeah, so has a great one
that you loved ever been cut?

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.850
- I mean, yeah, a lot of
stuff's been cut over the years.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.850
Sometimes you'll put one
up at the table read,

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.490
where they choose what'll
go to dress rehearsal

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.416
that never get picked.

00:02:52.416 --> 00:02:54.990
It was around Christmas
time when we wrote,

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.232
this was years back,

00:02:56.232 --> 00:02:59.242
when Trump was still
president at the time.

00:02:59.242 --> 00:03:00.075
(guest groans)

00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:00.908
And it was- (laughs)

00:03:00.908 --> 00:03:02.490
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.400
I was hesitant to even bring it up.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.400
(audience cheering)
(guests clapping)

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.182
I just heard. I heard-

00:03:13.182 --> 00:03:14.550
- Like it was just a sound.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.700
- I heard a sound, I'm like,
yep, I know, I know exactly.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.950
- [Kelly] It was just sound, from the gut.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.852
- But it was, that's so funny.

00:03:22.852 --> 00:03:25.116
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:25.116 --> 00:03:29.190
I just heard it, I'm like,
"Why did I even bring it up?"

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.210
- So wait, so that's happening.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.307
- Yeah, it was-

00:03:31.307 --> 00:03:32.410
- So there's a lot of material
there though, for SNL.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.080
- Yeah, it was a "Home Alone"

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.664
and Eric Trump was left
home alone in Trump Tower.

00:03:37.664 --> 00:03:38.790
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.860
And so, Don Jr. had to go back.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.680
and, "I gotta get back to
New York, Eric's home alone."

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.250
and there were like
investigators coming in,

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.490
in place of the burglars.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.810
- How did this get cut?

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.700
- I know, well it didn't even get picked

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.770
so it didn't even make it to the place

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.090
where it could be cut, but all
of Eric's traps didn't work.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.160
He was like hosing down the carpet

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.810
and we were a little bummed,

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:04.290
'cause you know, obviously
"Home Alone" is a classic, so.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.123
- It is a classic.

00:04:05.123 --> 00:04:07.530
- But you know, there's,
every week, there's stuff.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.270
- I know, I just noticed, I
was like, man, they get rid

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.770
of some funny stuff sometimes.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.570
- Yeah, you gotta come host.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.403
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:04:13.403 --> 00:04:14.717
- You'd be fantastic and do music.

00:04:14.717 --> 00:04:16.051
(audience cheering)
(Mikey clapping)

00:04:16.051 --> 00:04:19.554
- Here's the thing, I don't
think I'm funny like that.

00:04:19.554 --> 00:04:20.520
- You'd be awesome.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.590
- Like I can be witty at times,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:23.433
like just talking.
- [Mikey] You'd be awesome.

00:04:23.433 --> 00:04:24.840
- But, I don't think I'm funny like that.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.120
I did do a couple skits one time though,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.230
when I went to sing there.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.700
It was with Horatio.
- Oh, okay.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.710
- What's hard for me is, I laugh.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:33.168
- [Mikey] That's fine.

00:04:33.168 --> 00:04:34.146
- Like y'all, no it's not.
(Mikey laughs)

00:04:34.146 --> 00:04:35.400
No it's not, you're supposed to act,

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.840
you're supposed to like stay in character.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.060
But like, yeah. I don't know
how any of y'all held it down.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:41.370
I don't know if y'all saw Pedro Pascal,

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.919
when he was in the hospital
and (mimics nasal voice)

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.752
- [Mikey] Oh my God.

00:04:43.752 --> 00:04:45.283
- I was like-
- He was awesome.

00:04:45.283 --> 00:04:47.520
- I peed my pants, watching that.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.570
Like, how did you all not,

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.834
and you're all looking at
him like (mimics nasal voice)

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.882
and I was like, how are
they not laughing right now?

00:04:53.882 --> 00:04:56.970
- I mean, sometimes there will be sketches

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.130
and the camera will be on you

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.660
and then you'll try to keep it together

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.340
and then when the
camera's on someone else,

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.200
you'll start laughing, like especially-

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.100
- And then you screw them.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.440
- I know, but someone like Pedro,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.825
who was so good.
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh my God.

00:05:08.825 --> 00:05:09.658
It's so funny.
- But I think

00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:10.491
you would be fantastic.

00:05:10.491 --> 00:05:11.324
- You are very nice.

00:05:11.324 --> 00:05:12.293
- [Mikey] I mean it.

00:05:12.293 --> 00:05:13.174
(audience cheering)

00:05:13.174 --> 00:05:15.480
Well, it's time for another
commercial break, everybody.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.970
Saturday Night Live returns this weekend.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.650
You can watch on NBC and Peacock.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:24.650
We've got a touching story.
(audience members laughing)

